  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>Located in the heart of Munich, Germany, the New European College (NEC) was established in 2014. In collaboration with Wittenborg University of Applied Sciences, the college offers a modern, progressive approach to business education. By blending research-driven learning with real-world projects, the college prepares you for the demands of the modern business environment. The academic experience is distinctly international, combining the Dutch emphasis on practical learning with an American-style model of small, interactive classes; typically limited to 25 students.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student life",
      "value": "<p>At New European College, you will be part of an international community that values interactive learning. The campus atmosphere is designed to be inclusive and supportive, with a focus on your personal and professional growth. The college actively helps you transition to life in Munich, ensuring you feel at home while pursuing your studies.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>Finding a place to live is a key part of your study abroad experience, and NEC is here to help. The college partners with local housing agencies and student dormitories to assist you in locating comfortable and modern accommodation. Once you receive provisional acceptance, an Accommodation Officer will guide you through the process, providing you with resources and housing opportunities to help you settle into Munich quickly.</p><p><i>Additionally, if you’re looking for budget-friendly accommodation options outside the campus, feel free to </i><a href=\"https://edvoy.com/app/\"><i>download our app</i></a><i> and check out the Stays feature!</i></p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Facilities",
      "value": "<ul><li><strong>Academic environment:</strong> The college utilizes a contemporary block-style academic schedule, allowing you to begin your studies six times per year.</li><li><strong>Support services:</strong> You have access to administrative and career services designed to help you navigate your academic journey and identify professional opportunities.</li><li><strong>Library</strong>: At NEC, you have access to a wide range of academic resources through the college’s e-library and digital databases. These include over 5000 e-books and 10,000 e-magazines.</li></ul>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Campuses",
      "value": "<p><strong>Munich:</strong> The college is situated in Munich, Germany. This location provides you with access to a vibrant city atmosphere and serves as a hub for your business-focused education.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    }
